        "conceptual_move": "The distance along a round sphere is its central angle",
        "boundary": "This identifies the induced length distance of a positive-dimensional unit sphere. It leaves the ambient chord metric unchanged; for antipodal points these two distances are \\(2\\) and \\(\\pi\\). The condition \\(n>0\\) is essential for arbitrary endpoint pairs: the two-point sphere has no continuous internal path between its two distinct points. It supplies no global Riemannian bundle instance, general manifold geodesic-existence theorem, transport estimate, stochastic result, or textbook chapter completion. Spherical transport is a possible consumer of the distance identity.",
